<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catechetical School of Alexandria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Catechetical School of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> was a centre of Christian teaching in Alexandria from the late second century. Under Pantaenus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clement-of-alexandria">Clement of Alexandria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/origen">Origen</a> it combined instruction in the faith with Greek philosophy and the allegorical reading of scripture. It strongly shaped the early theology of the Greek-speaking church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catechetical-school-of-alexandria.jpg" alt="Catechetical School of Alexandria" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was ThutmoseIII at English Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cairo_mosques.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
